umbriel (A Wayland compositor built on wlroots)
===============================================

umbriel is a modern Wayland compositor / tiling window manager for daily
use: scrolling, dwindle, master and stacking layouts, per-output
workspaces, window rules, blur, shadows, rounded corners, fluid
animations, HDR and variable refresh rate. It is written in C++23 and
built on wlroots 0.20 with an in-tree scene-graph/renderer fork called
umbrielfx.

Upstream: https://github.com/noctalia-dev/umbriel
License: MIT

DEPENDENCIES
============
Build/runtime (Slackware -current core, not listed in REQUIRES):
  wlroots-0.20, wayland (+wayland-protocols), libinput, libei, pixman,
  libdrm, libdisplay-info, cairo, pango, libxcb (xrender/xshape/xcb-icccm/
  xcb-ewmh/xcb-xfixes/xcb-xtest), libxkbcommon, glibc

Requires from SlackBuilds.org (listed in REQUIRES):
  tomlplusplus  (TOML config parser, header-only)

Note on nlohmann/json: Umbriel calls dependency('nlohmann_json') and
resolves it on this system even though the packaged nlohmann-json does not
ship a .pc file; meson's CMake backend finds its config package. If a
fresh build cannot find nlohmann_json, add its CMake config to the meson
subprojects wraps, or install a variant that provides a .pc file.

Optional build features (default auto; skipped here when the lib is
absent):
  jemalloc     - used automatically on glibc if the dev package is present
  libsystemd   - skipped (not installed); the localed keymap lookup is
                 disabled and keyboards fall back to libxkbcommon defaults

BUILD RUNTIME (optional, not used):
  Xwayland     - needed at runtime for X11 apps (spawned on demand)
  xdg-desktop-portal-umbriel - screen sharing portal backend

BUILDING
========
  source ./umbriel.info
  wget -O umbriel-0.1.0.tar.gz "$DOWNLOAD"
  md5sum -c <(echo "$MD5SUM  umbriel-0.1.0.tar.gz")
  ./umbriel.SlackBuild

The build configures Meson with the final /usr prefix (the datadir path is
compiled in, so it must not be changed afterward) and disables the unit
test / harness targets.

RUNNING
=======
Select "umbriel" in your display manager, or run:
  start-umbriel
Configuration is copied from examples/config.toml to
~/.config/umbriel/config.toml (the package ships the packaged default).
The default keybind example spawns "kitty", which is not a hard dependency.
